# Rules for the archive EAS Build uploads to its build workers.
#
# Why this file exists: EAS CLI archives the project by copying every file except those matched by
# .gitignore — and `expo/.gitignore` ignores `google-services.json`, the Firebase Android config the
# deploy workflow writes from the FIREBASE_GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON secret. Ignored means "not uploaded",
# so the worker received a project whose app.json points at a file that was never there, and the build
# failed before it compiled anything. `.easignore` is EAS's own escape hatch: it is used *instead of*
# every .gitignore file in the repository, so the file can be kept out of Git (it is a credential) while
# still reaching the build. Source: https://expo.fyi/eas-build-archive
#
#   *** KEEP THIS FILE IN STEP WITH THE .gitignore FILES ***
# Once .easignore exists, no .gitignore is consulted anywhere in the repository — not the root one,
# not expo/.gitignore. Any rule added to either of those must be copied here too, or EAS will upload
# that path. The only deliberate differences are google-services.json and GoogleService-Info.plist
# at the bottom of this file.
#
# Notably: the local .env, .env.local, .env.vercel, .neon.txt and .data entries below are secrets that
# live on developer machines. They are restated here for exactly that reason — a build run from a
# laptop would otherwise upload them.

# --- root .gitignore, restated ---
node_modules
.next
out
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.vercel
.neon.txt
.data
*.log
.DS_Store
.neon

.vercel

# Vercel CLI deploy transcript / workflow scratch files
vercel-out.txt
eas-build.log
eas-build.json
eas-whoami.log
eas-view.json
eas-view.err

# EAS build artifacts produced locally (never upload back to EAS)
expo/dist
expo/web-build
expo/ios
expo/android
expo/.expo
expo/node_modules

# --- expo/.gitignore, restated ---
# (node_modules, .env, *.log and .DS_Store from the block above already match their expo/ twins,
#  because a rule without a slash matches that name at any depth)
.claude/preflight-logs/
expo/.claude/preflight-logs/

# --- deliberately NOT ignored ---
# google-services.json is written by the "Install Firebase Android configuration" step in
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml and must be inside the uploaded archive: app.json declares it as
# android.googleServicesFile. iOS uses GoogleService-Info.plist for FCM on iOS (written from the
# FIREBASE_GOOGLE_SERVICE_INFO_PLIST secret when an iOS build is requested). Both stay out of Git
# (expo/.gitignore still ignores them for the working tree), and the archive itself is transferred
# over TLS to Expo's private storage.
!google-services.json
!GoogleService-Info.plist
